# Styles: For style, a named style that elements ask for with Style, one or several at a time.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Styles · For style
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: note
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 12 0
				Padding: 8 10
				Background: tint
		For style: warning
			Box:
				Background: #FBEAE8
				Border: 0 0 0 3
				Border color: #A32D2D
			Typography:
				Bold: true
		For style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 60%
	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: For style
		Paragraph: A `For style` rule applies to the elements that name it in their `Style`. An element can name several, separated by spaces. When two of its styles give the same property, the rule written later in `Styles` wins: `warning` comes after `note`, so its background wins.
			Style: intro
		Text: Style: note
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Delivery takes two weeks from the date of the order.
			Style: note
		Text: Style: note narrow
			Style: label
		Paragraph: The same note, with the width of the narrow style added.
			Style: note narrow
		Text: Style: note warning
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Switch off the power before removing the cover.
			Style: note warning
		Text: Style: warning note  (the order in Style does not matter)
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Switch off the power before removing the cover.
			Style: warning note
